    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d310">

                <pb facs="0587" n="453" sameAs="frus:frus1888p1/pg453"/>

                <head>No. 310.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bayard to Mr. Pak Chung
                    Yang.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1888-01-10"><hi rendition="#italic">January</hi> 10,
                        1888</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I had the honor to receive to-day by the
                    hands of your secretary your note of this date, whereby you are pleased to
                    inform me that you have been appointed His Corean Majesty’s envoy extraordinary
                    and minister plenipotentiary near this Government, and that you are prepared to
                    enter upon the discharge of your duties as soon as it shall please the President
                    to grant you an audience and receive your credentials, to which end you solicit
                    an interview with me.</p>
                <pb facs="0588" n="454" xml:id="pg454"/>
                <p>I have the honor to inform you in reply that, as I have already advised your
                    secretary, I shall be happy to receive you on Friday next, the 18th instant, at
                    12 o’clock, noon, and arrange to accompany you thereafter at an early day to
                    present your credentials to the President.</p>
                <p>Accept, sir, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">T. F. Bayard.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
